# GPUI's web platform shares WebAssembly memory with worker threads, which
# browsers only allow on cross-origin isolated pages. Requests to Mattermost
# servers are CORS fetches, which isolation allows.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer

# The page is checked on every load; it names the app's files, which
# scripts/web names by their content, so the browser keeps those for good
# (and Chrome reuses the compiled app). sw.js, which keeps the app's files
# in the browser's copy, and the demo keep their names, so they are checked
# each time.
/*.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/matty/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/matty/matty-web*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/matty/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/*.gz
  Cache-Control: no-cache
